    skos:altLabel "InvestmentChoiceDecision" ;
    skos:definition "A corporate reputation influence situation is defined as a function that supports a specific continuant and influences an investment decision. A corporate reputation influence situation qualifies as a function precisely when it supports a specific continuant and influences an investment decision. The support of a specific continuant and the influence on an investment decision are jointly performed by a corporate reputation influence situation functioning as a function." ;
    skos:broader <https://signals.zndx.org/sdg#SDG_ICE> ;
    skos:inScheme <https://signals.zndx.org/sdg/scheme> .

