    skos:altLabel "Investor Communication" ;
    skos:altLabel "Shareholder Relations" ;
    skos:altLabel "Investor Engagement" ;
    skos:altLabel "Capital Market Communication" ;
    skos:definition "This term covers organizational activities that manage communication channels between a company and its institutional investors. Practitioners organize earnings calls, distribute quarterly reports, and coordinate shareholder meetings to maintain transparent financial dialogue. These activities ensure consistent information flow regarding corporate performance and strategic direction. An organizational activity is defined as the management of communication and relationships between a company and its investors. The organizational activity functions by managing the communication and relationships that connect a company to its investors. Applies to organizational activities managing communication channels between a company and its institutional investors." ;
    skos:broader <https://signals.zndx.org/sdg#SDG_GENERIC> ;
    skos:inScheme <https://signals.zndx.org/sdg/scheme> .

<https://signals.zndx.org/sdg#SDG_MATERIAL_ENTITY_KEYFRAME_TIMELINE> a skos:Concept ;
