    skos:altLabel "animation timeline" ;
    skos:altLabel "keyframe track" ;
    skos:altLabel "motion timeline" ;
    skos:altLabel "keyframe sequence" ;
    skos:definition "This term represents the temporal interval that marks specific time points for keyframes within an animation sequence. It captures the structured timeline where visual changes or motions are anchored at precise moments. Practitioners use it to organize and synchronize animation elements in digital media production. A temporal interval is defined as the element that designates the precise time points for keyframes within an animation sequence. The specific time points for keyframes in an animation sequence are established by a temporal interval. Used in animation and video editing to define the temporal interval that marks specific time points for keyframes in a sequence." ;
    skos:broader <https://signals.zndx.org/sdg#SDG_MATERIAL_ENTITY> ;
    skos:inScheme <https://signals.zndx.org/sdg/scheme> .

<https://signals.zndx.org/sdg#SDG_MATERIAL_ENTITY_LATERAL_RESTRAINT_STRAP> a skos:Concept ;
