    skos:altLabel "Market Direction Shift" ;
    skos:altLabel "Financial Trend Indicator" ;
    skos:altLabel "Price Movement Signal" ;
    skos:definition "A financial data point that tracks the directional change or pattern of a stock over time. Analysts use these indicators to identify long-term growth or decline patterns in market behavior. A financial value serves as the indicator of the directional change or pattern that a stock exhibits over time. (Definitional) The directional change or pattern of a stock over time is indicated by a financial value. (Relational-fronted) Applies to financial data points that track the directional change or pattern of a stock over time. Analysts use these indicators to identify long-term growth or decline patterns." ;
    skos:broader <https://signals.zndx.org/sdg#SDG_QUALITY> ;
    skos:inScheme <https://signals.zndx.org/sdg/scheme> .

<https://signals.zndx.org/sdg#SDG_ICE_DIRECTIVE_MARKETING_PLAN> a skos:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "Marketing Plan" ;
    skos:notation "3.2.6" ;
    skos:altLabel "MARKETING_PLAN" ;
    skos:altLabel "Promotional Strategy Plan" ;
    skos:altLabel "Marketing Strategy Document" ;
    skos:altLabel "Promotional Activity Plan" ;
    skos:altLabel "Commercial Marketing Plan" ;
    skos:altLabel "Marketing Strategy Outline" ;
    skos:definition "A marketing plan outlines promotional strategies and commercial activities designed to achieve specific business objectives. This strategic document coordinates advertising campaigns, market positioning, and customer engagement initiatives to drive commercial success. A plan is defined as a document that outlines the promotional strategies and activities for a commercial initiative. The promotional strategies and activities for a commercial initiative are outlined by a plan. A marketing plan outlines promotional strategies and commercial activities designed to achieve specific business objectives. This strategic document coordinates advertising campaigns, market positioning, and customer engagement initiatives to drive commercial success." ;
    skos:broader <https://signals.zndx.org/sdg#SDG_ICE_DIRECTIVE> ;
    skos:inScheme <https://signals.zndx.org/sdg/scheme> .

<https://signals.zndx.org/sdg#SDG_ICE_DESIGNATIVE_MATHEMATICAL_CONCEPT> a skos:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "Mathematical Concept" ;
    skos:notation "3.3.4" ;
    skos:altLabel "MATHEMATICAL_CONCEPT" ;
    skos:altLabel "Mathematical Concept" ;
    skos:altLabel "Math Concept" ;
    skos:altLabel "Mathematical Theory" ;
    skos:altLabel "Quantitative Concept" ;
    skos:altLabel "Mathematical Principle" ;
    skos:definition "A mathematical concept represents an abstract principle that underpins mathematical reasoning and quantitative analysis. These foundational ideas enable systematic problem-solving and support the development of algorithms and computational models. A subject concept functions as the foundational basis for mathematical reasoning and abstract quantitative relationships. (Definitional) Mathematical reasoning and abstract quantitative relationships are underpinned by a subject concept. (Relational-fronted) A mathematical concept represents an abstract principle that underpins mathematical reasoning and quantitative analysis. These foundational ideas enable systematic problem-solving and support the development of algorithms and computational models." ;
    skos:broader <https://signals.zndx.org/sdg#SDG_ICE_DESIGNATIVE> ;
    skos:inScheme <https://signals.zndx.org/sdg/scheme> .

<https://signals.zndx.org/sdg#SDG_ICE_DESCRIPTIVE_MEASUREMENT_PARAMETER> a skos:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "Measurement Parameter" ;
    skos:notation "3.1.19" ;
    skos:altLabel "MEASUREMENT_PARAMETER" ;
    skos:altLabel "measurement parameter" ;
    skos:altLabel "quantified property" ;
    skos:altLabel "measurement dimension" ;
    skos:altLabel "physical measurement parameter" ;
    skos:altLabel "property quantifier" ;
    skos:definition "A measurement parameter specifies the exact physical property or dimension targeted during quantification, linking the abstract concept of a property to a concrete measurement unit. Practitioners employ this term when documenting experimental setups, calibration protocols, or data collection instruments that capture specific physical quantities. The parameter anchors the measurement process to a well-defined physical attribute, ensuring consistency across observations and repeatability in scientific reporting. A measurement unit is defined as that which quantifies a specific physical property or dimension. The quantification of a specific physical property or dimension is carried out by a measurement unit. Used in metrology and physical sciences to denote a specific property or dimension being measured, such as temperature, mass, or length, along with its associated unit and quantification method." ;
    skos:broader <https://signals.zndx.org/sdg#SDG_ICE_DESCRIPTIVE> ;
    skos:inScheme <https://signals.zndx.org/sdg/scheme> .

<https://signals.zndx.org/sdg#SDG_ROLE_MEMBER> a skos:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "Member" ;
    skos:notation "5.59" ;
    skos:altLabel "MEMBER" ;
    skos:altLabel "Group Member" ;
    skos:altLabel "Organization Member" ;
    skos:altLabel "Association Member" ;
    skos:altLabel "Member Participant" ;
    skos:altLabel "Organizational Member" ;
    skos:definition "Member entities confer participation and benefit eligibility within groups or organizations. Membership rosters and access control systems record these participations to manage group privileges and organizational resources. An organization member role is defined as the condition that confers participation and benefit eligibility within a group. Within a group, participation and benefit eligibility are conferred by an organization member role. Member entities confer participation and benefit eligibility within groups or organizations. Membership rosters and access control systems record these participations to manage group privileges and organizational resources." ;
    skos:broader <https://signals.zndx.org/sdg#SDG_ROLE> ;
    skos:inScheme <https://signals.zndx.org/sdg/scheme> .

<https://signals.zndx.org/sdg#SDG_PROCESS_MEMBERSHIP> a skos:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "Membership" ;
    skos:notation "1.101" ;
    skos:altLabel "MEMBERSHIP" ;
    skos:altLabel "Organizational affiliation" ;
    skos:altLabel "Group membership status" ;
    skos:altLabel "Institutional affiliation" ;
    skos:altLabel "Community membership record" ;
    skos:altLabel "Membership enrollment" ;
    skos:definition "An act of social group membership that establishes an individual's formal affiliation with an organization. This term captures the formal process and resulting status of joining an organization. It encompasses the rights, responsibilities, and identity associated with being a member. The act of social group membership is the specific action that establishes an individual's formal affiliation with an organization. The concept denoted is an act of social group membership, defined as the mechanism that establishes an individual's formal affiliation with an organization. Applies to records and statuses that formalize an individual's connection to an organization or group." ;
    skos:broader <https://signals.zndx.org/sdg#SDG_PROCESS> ;
    skos:inScheme <https://signals.zndx.org/sdg/scheme> .

<https://signals.zndx.org/sdg#SDG_MATERIAL_ENTITY_MINOR_PERSON> a skos:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "Minor Person" ;
    skos:notation "2.2.36" ;
    skos:altLabel "MINOR_PERSON" ;
    skos:altLabel "Young person" ;
    skos:altLabel "Underage individual" ;
    skos:altLabel "Youth demographic" ;
    skos:altLabel "Legal minor" ;
    skos:altLabel "Juvenile person" ;
    skos:definition "A person who falls under the youth demographic and has an age below the legal age of majority. This term identifies individuals who are legally recognized as minors and require specific protections and considerations. It is used in legal, social, and educational contexts to denote age-related status. A person satisfies this condition by belonging to the youth demographic and maintaining an age beneath the legal age of majority. (Procedural/conditional) The youth demographic classification and an age below the legal age of majority jointly characterize a person. (Relational-fronted) Applies to individuals who have not reached the legal age of majority and are subject to specific legal protections." ;
    skos:broader <https://signals.zndx.org/sdg#SDG_MATERIAL_ENTITY> ;
    skos:inScheme <https://signals.zndx.org/sdg/scheme> .

<https://signals.zndx.org/sdg#SDG_MATERIAL_ENTITY_PATIENT> a skos:Concept ;
