    skos:altLabel "Predicate Representation" ;
    skos:altLabel "Constructed Predicate" ;
    skos:altLabel "Predicate Information Content" ;
    skos:altLabel "Predicate Entity" ;
    skos:definition "A predicate concept expresses constructed predicates to define relationships and properties within knowledge systems. This representational information content entity structures semantic relationships by establishing predicate definitions, mapping conceptual connections, and enabling precise knowledge representation through formalized predicate expressions. A representational information content entity is defined as a construct that expresses a constructed predicate. The expression of a constructed predicate is a direct attribute of any representational information content entity. Representational information content entities that express constructed predicates to define relationships and properties within knowledge systems." ;
    skos:broader <https://signals.zndx.org/sdg#SDG_ICE> ;
    skos:inScheme <https://signals.zndx.org/sdg/scheme> .

<https://signals.zndx.org/sdg#SDG_GENERIC_PREVALENCE_RATE> a skos:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "Prevalence Rate" ;
    skos:notation "0.19" ;
    skos:altLabel "PREVALENCE_RATE" ;
    skos:altLabel "Prevalence Frequency" ;
    skos:altLabel "Population Proportion" ;
    skos:altLabel "Condition Rate" ;
    skos:altLabel "Disease Frequency" ;
    skos:altLabel "Health Indicator Rate" ;
    skos:definition "A prevalence rate represents the proportion of individuals in a specified population who have a particular condition or characteristic at a given time. It is used in epidemiology and public health to assess the burden of disease or the distribution of traits. The rate provides a snapshot of health status within the population, enabling researchers and policymakers to understand the scope of health issues and allocate resources effectively. A frequency is defined as the proportion of individuals within a specified population who possess a particular condition or characteristic at a given time. (Definitional) The proportion of individuals in a specified population who have a particular condition or characteristic at a given time serves as the representation of a frequency. (Rel This rate represents the proportion of individuals in a specified population who have a particular condition or characteristic at a given time. It is used in epidemiology and public health to assess the burden of " ;
    skos:broader <https://signals.zndx.org/sdg#SDG_GENERIC> ;
    skos:inScheme <https://signals.zndx.org/sdg/scheme> .

<https://signals.zndx.org/sdg#SDG_PROCESS_PROGRAM_OF_STUDY> a skos:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "Program Of Study" ;
    skos:notation "1.104" ;
    skos:altLabel "PROGRAM_OF_STUDY" ;
    skos:altLabel "program of study" ;
    skos:altLabel "degree program" ;
    skos:altLabel "academic curriculum track" ;
    skos:altLabel "educational program" ;
    skos:altLabel "study plan" ;
    skos:definition "A structured course of educational instruction designed to lead to the attainment of an academic degree. This educational framework outlines the required coursework, credit hours, and milestones necessary for degree completion. The program organizes learning activities to ensure comprehensive knowledge acquisition and skill development aligned with degree requirements. A structured course of educational instruction is a formalized sequence of teaching formulated to facilitate the acquisition of an academic degree. The attainment of an academic degree serves as the designated outcome of a structured course of A structured course of educational instruction designed to lead to the attainment of an academic degree. This educational framework outlines the required coursework, credit hours, and milestones necessary for degree completion." ;
    skos:broader <https://signals.zndx.org/sdg#SDG_PROCESS> ;
    skos:inScheme <https://signals.zndx.org/sdg/scheme> .

<https://signals.zndx.org/sdg#SDG_ROLE_PROPERTY_OWNER> a skos:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "Property Owner" ;
    skos:notation "5.60" ;
    skos:altLabel "PROPERTY_OWNER" ;
    skos:altLabel "property owner" ;
    skos:altLabel "asset holder" ;
    skos:altLabel "landowner" ;
    skos:altLabel "property titleholder" ;
    skos:altLabel "real estate owner" ;
    skos:definition "This term identifies the individual or entity that legally holds ownership rights to a specific property or asset. It captures the formal relationship of possession and control over real estate or tangible assets. Practitioners use it to document legal titles, responsibilities, and asset management records. An occupation role constitutes the position borne by an individual or entity that legally possesses rights to a specific property or asset. The individual or entity that legally possesses rights to a specific property or asset is the holder Used when identifying the individual or entity that legally possesses rights to a specific property or asset." ;
    skos:broader <https://signals.zndx.org/sdg#SDG_ROLE> ;
    skos:inScheme <https://signals.zndx.org/sdg/scheme> .

<https://signals.zndx.org/sdg#SDG_MATERIAL_ENTITY_PUBLIC_INFORMATION_OFFICER> a skos:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "Public Information Officer" ;
    skos:notation "2.2.38" ;
    skos:altLabel "PUBLIC_INFORMATION_OFFICER" ;
    skos:altLabel "PublicInformationOfficer" ;
    skos:definition "The government organization role designated for overseeing public information and media relations entails the management and dissemination of such content. Managing and disseminating public information and media relations constitutes the operational duties of a government organization role. A government organization role is defined by its responsibility to manage and disseminate public information and media relations." ;
    skos:broader <https://signals.zndx.org/sdg#SDG_MATERIAL_ENTITY> ;
    skos:inScheme <https://signals.zndx.org/sdg/scheme> .

<https://signals.zndx.org/sdg#SDG_QUALITY_QO_S_CONSTRAINT> a skos:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "Qo S Constraint" ;
    skos:notation "4.3" ;
    skos:altLabel "QO_S_CONSTRAINT" ;
    skos:altLabel "Quality Constraint" ;
    skos:altLabel "Service Performance Constraint" ;
    skos:altLabel "QoS Constraint" ;
    skos:altLabel "Service Quality Constraint" ;
    skos:definition "A quality specification that defines acceptable performance limits for a service. This constraint constrains service performance to ensure compliance with specified metrics. A quality specification is defined as the set of acceptable performance limits or requirements that apply to a service within an agreement. A quality specification that defines acceptable performance limits for a service." ;
    skos:broader <https://signals.zndx.org/sdg#SDG_QUALITY> ;
    skos:inScheme <https://signals.zndx.org/sdg/scheme> .

<https://signals.zndx.org/sdg#SDG_ICE_DIRECTIVE_QUALITY_IMPROVEMENT_FRAMEWORK> a skos:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "Quality Improvement Framework" ;
    skos:notation "3.2.7" ;
    skos:altLabel "QUALITY_IMPROVEMENT_FRAMEWORK" ;
    skos:altLabel "QualityImprovementFramework" ;
    skos:definition "A structured quality specification is an entity that provides a systematic approach for the planning and execution of quality improvement initiatives. The planning and execution of quality improvement initiatives proceed according to the systematic approach provided by a structured quality specification. A structured quality specification relates to quality improvement initiatives through the systematic approach it provides for their planning and execution." ;
    skos:broader <https://signals.zndx.org/sdg#SDG_ICE_DIRECTIVE> ;
    skos:inScheme <https://signals.zndx.org/sdg/scheme> .

<https://signals.zndx.org/sdg#SDG_MATERIAL_ENTITY_QUANTITATIVE_ANALYTIC_TOOL> a skos:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "Quantitative Analytic Tool" ;
    skos:notation "2.2.39" ;
    skos:altLabel "QUANTITATIVE_ANALYTIC_TOOL" ;
    skos:altLabel "Numerical Analysis Instrument" ;
    skos:altLabel "Statistical Calculation Device" ;
    skos:altLabel "Data Quantification Tool" ;
    skos:altLabel "Research Measurement Instrument" ;
    skos:altLabel "Analytical Calculation Program" ;
    skos:definition "The quantitative analytic tool functions as a research artifact designed specifically for performing numerical analysis and data interpretation. Practitioners utilize these tools to calculate statistical measures, process numerical datasets, and generate quantitative research outcomes. The instruments support systematic data examination procedures that require precise numerical computation and analytical processing capabilities. A tool is defined by this description when it is specifically designed or utilized to perform numerical analysis and data interpretation within a clinical or research context. Numerical analysis and data interpretation within a clinical or research context are executed by a tool that is specifically designed or utilized for that function. This term applies to instruments designed for performing numerical analysis and data interpretation within clinical or research settings." ;
    skos:broader <https://signals.zndx.org/sdg#SDG_MATERIAL_ENTITY> ;
    skos:inScheme <https://signals.zndx.org/sdg/scheme> .

<https://signals.zndx.org/sdg#SDG_GENERIC_RAFFLE_CONDUCTING_ACTIVITY> a skos:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "Raffle Conducting Activity" ;
    skos:notation "0.20" ;
    skos:altLabel "RAFFLE_CONDUCTING_ACTIVITY" ;
    skos:altLabel "Raffle Conducting Activity" ;
    skos:altLabel "Raffle Organization Activity" ;
    skos:altLabel "Raffle Execution Activity" ;
    skos:altLabel "Fundraising Raffle Activity" ;
    skos:altLabel "Raffle Management Activity" ;
    skos:definition "Raffle conducting activity is an organizational activity that involves conducting a raffle. This activity encompasses the planning, organization, and execution of a raffle draw, often aimed at raising funds or promoting an organization or event. The process of arranging and conducting a raffle draw constitutes the core of this organizational activity, which operates for fundraising or promotional purposes. This organizational activity maintains a central focus on organizing and executing a raffle draw, with its designated purpose being fundraising or promotion. Used for organizational activities that involve organizing and executing a raffle, often for fundraising or promotional purposes." ;
    skos:broader <https://signals.zndx.org/sdg#SDG_GENERIC> ;
    skos:inScheme <https://signals.zndx.org/sdg/scheme> .

<https://signals.zndx.org/sdg#SDG_MATERIAL_ENTITY_RECEIVING_FACILITY_STAFF> a skos:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "Receiving Facility Staff" ;
    skos:notation "2.2.40" ;
    skos:altLabel "RECEIVING_FACILITY_STAFF" ;
    skos:altLabel "Receiving Center Personnel" ;
    skos:altLabel "Facility Intake Staff" ;
    skos:altLabel "Healthcare Reception Team" ;
    skos:altLabel "Notification Processing Staff" ;
    skos:altLabel "Facility Intake Personnel" ;
    skos:definition "Receiving facility staff function as healthcare facility employees responsible for managing the intake of communicable disease notifications. These personnel process incoming reports through established facility workflows to ensure proper documentation and follow-up procedures. The staff members operate within facility administrative structures to coordinate notification handling and maintain compliance with reporting requirements. This term applies to personnel employed by healthcare facilities who manage the intake and processing of incoming communicable disease notifications." ;
    skos:broader <https://signals.zndx.org/sdg#SDG_MATERIAL_ENTITY> ;
    skos:inScheme <https://signals.zndx.org/sdg/scheme> .

<https://signals.zndx.org/sdg#SDG_INDEPENDENT_CONTINUANT_RECOVERED_STATE> a skos:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "Recovered State" ;
    skos:notation "2.12" ;
    skos:altLabel "RECOVERED_STATE" ;
    skos:altLabel "Post-Deficiency Recovery State" ;
    skos:altLabel "Restored Health State" ;
    skos:altLabel "Recovered Nutritional Status" ;
    skos:altLabel "Health Recovery Phase" ;
    skos:altLabel "Post-Illness Restoration" ;
    skos:definition "A constituent state representing the successful restoration of health or nutritional status following a period of deficiency or illness. The state captures the moment when clinical markers, dietary intake, or physiological indicators confirm that the entity has moved beyond the vulnerable condition and achieved stable recovery. This state marks the point where health metrics or nutritional indicators return to baseline levels after a prior deficiency or illness. The constituent state appears in clinical monitoring, public health tracking, and nutritional rehabilitation programs where recovery is measured against prior vulnerable conditions." ;
    skos:broader <https://signals.zndx.org/sdg#SDG_INDEPENDENT_CONTINUANT> ;
    skos:inScheme <https://signals.zndx.org/sdg/scheme> .

<https://signals.zndx.org/sdg#SDG_PROCESS_SERVICE_MANAGEMENT_PROCESS> a skos:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "Service Management Process" ;
    skos:notation "1.105" ;
    skos:altLabel "SERVICE_MANAGEMENT_PROCESS" ;
    skos:altLabel "Service Management Process" ;
    skos:altLabel "Service Provision Coordination" ;
    skos:altLabel "Service Orchestration Process" ;
    skos:altLabel "Service Delivery Workflow" ;
    skos:altLabel "Service Management Workflow" ;
    skos:definition "A telemetry process that coordinates the provision of a service type. This concept represents the structured set of activities and controls used to manage the delivery, performance, and improvement of a specific service, ensuring alignment with service level agreements and operational goals. A telemetry process is defined as a process that coordinates the provision of a service type. The coordination of the provision of a service type is performed by a telemetry process. Applies to processes that coordinate the delivery and management of services within an organization." ;
    skos:broader <https://signals.zndx.org/sdg#SDG_PROCESS> ;
    skos:inScheme <https://signals.zndx.org/sdg/scheme> .

<https://signals.zndx.org/sdg#SDG_ICE_DIRECTIVE_SERVICE_PERFORMANCE_METRIC> a skos:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "Service Performance Metric" ;
    skos:notation "3.2.8" ;
    skos:altLabel "SERVICE_PERFORMANCE_METRIC" ;
    skos:altLabel "Service performance metric" ;
    skos:altLabel "Service performance specification" ;
    skos:altLabel "Service metric" ;
    skos:altLabel "Performance specification for services" ;
    skos:altLabel "Service type performance measure" ;
    skos:definition "This term identifies a performance specification used to evaluate the operational metrics of a service type. It quantifies attributes such as response time, throughput, or reliability to ensure service quality standards are met. A performance specification is defined as a measure for the performance of a service type. The performance of a service type is measured by a performance specification. Use this term for specifications that quantify how a service type performs against established criteria. It applies when the focus is on measuring service quality or efficiency, not on general performance constraints or clinical data." ;
    skos:broader <https://signals.zndx.org/sdg#SDG_ICE_DIRECTIVE> ;
    skos:inScheme <https://signals.zndx.org/sdg/scheme> .

<https://signals.zndx.org/sdg#SDG_MATERIAL_ENTITY_SERVICE_PROVIDER> a skos:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "Service Provider" ;
    skos:notation "2.2.41" ;
    skos:altLabel "SERVICE_PROVIDER" ;
    skos:altLabel "ServiceProvider" ;
    skos:definition "A material entity is defined as an entity that provides a service function. A service function is provided by a material entity. A material entity serves as the provider of a service function." ;
    skos:broader <https://signals.zndx.org/sdg#SDG_MATERIAL_ENTITY> ;
    skos:inScheme <https://signals.zndx.org/sdg/scheme> .

<https://signals.zndx.org/sdg#SDG_PROCESS_SERVICE_PROVISION_ACTIVITY> a skos:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "Service Provision Activity" ;
    skos:notation "1.106" ;
    skos:altLabel "SERVICE_PROVISION_ACTIVITY" ;
    skos:altLabel "Service Provision Activity" ;
    skos:altLabel "Service Delivery" ;
    skos:altLabel "Service Provision" ;
    skos:altLabel "Service Execution" ;
    skos:altLabel "Client Service Activity" ;
    skos:definition "A process that delivers a service type to a client. This term applies when an organization executes a specific service offering, involving the direct interaction between the provider and the recipient to fulfill a contractual or agreed-upon obligation. A process is defined as the delivery of a service type. A process executes the delivery of a service type. Tracks the delivery of a service type to a client. Used to document the execution of service agreements." ;
    skos:broader <https://signals.zndx.org/sdg#SDG_PROCESS> ;
    skos:inScheme <https://signals.zndx.org/sdg/scheme> .

<https://signals.zndx.org/sdg#SDG_PROCESS_SERVICE_REQUEST> a skos:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "Service Request" ;
    skos:notation "1.107" ;
    skos:altLabel "SERVICE_REQUEST" ;
    skos:altLabel "Service function request" ;
    skos:altLabel "Service request act" ;
    skos:altLabel "Act of requesting service" ;
    skos:altLabel "Service function request act" ;
    skos:definition "An act of Requesting that seeks a Service Function. The act formally requests the provision of a specific service function. An act of requesting is defined as an entity that requests a service function. The requesting relation links each act of requesting to a service function. An act of requesting that seeks a service function." ;
    skos:broader <https://signals.zndx.org/sdg#SDG_PROCESS> ;
    skos:inScheme <https://signals.zndx.org/sdg/scheme> .

<https://signals.zndx.org/sdg#SDG_ICE_DESCRIPTIVE_SIGNIFICANCE_LEVEL> a skos:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "Significance Level" ;
    skos:notation "3.1.20" ;
    skos:altLabel "SIGNIFICANCE_LEVEL" ;
    skos:altLabel "Significance Level" ;
    skos:altLabel "Statistical Significance Indicator" ;
    skos:altLabel "Confidence Level Measure" ;
    skos:altLabel "Statistical Qualification Metric" ;
    skos:altLabel "Significance Threshold" ;
    skos:definition "A ratio measurement information content entity that indicates the statistical significance of a qualification level. This concept represents the threshold value used in hypothesis testing to determine whether an observed effect is statistically significant, typically expressed as a p-value or alpha level. A ratio measurement information content entity functions to indicate the statistical significance of a qualification level. (Functional/Procedural) The statistical significance of a qualification level is indicated by a ratio measurement information content entity. (Relational-fronted) Applies to statistical analysis where the probability of observing a result by chance is quantified." ;
    skos:broader <https://signals.zndx.org/sdg#SDG_ICE_DESCRIPTIVE> ;
    skos:inScheme <https://signals.zndx.org/sdg/scheme> .

<https://signals.zndx.org/sdg#SDG_DISPOSITION_SIMULATION_SOFTWARE> a skos:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "Simulation Software" ;
    skos:notation "6.2" ;
    skos:altLabel "SIMULATION_SOFTWARE" ;
    skos:altLabel "Simulation Software" ;
    skos:altLabel "Simulation Execution Tool" ;
    skos:altLabel "Simulation Computing Artifact" ;
    skos:altLabel "Simulation Modeling Software" ;
    skos:altLabel "Simulation Execution Environment" ;
    skos:definition "A computing artifact function that runs mathematical models to replicate the behavior of complex systems under varying conditions. This software executes simulation models by processing input parameters, calculating system responses, and generating output data that reflects the simulated environment's dynamics. A computing artifact function is defined as the entity that executes an artifact model specifically for simulation purposes. The execution of an artifact model for simulation purposes is carried out by a computing artifact function. Applies to the computing artifact function that runs mathematical models to replicate the behavior of complex systems under varying conditions." ;
    skos:broader <https://signals.zndx.org/sdg#SDG_DISPOSITION> ;
    skos:inScheme <https://signals.zndx.org/sdg/scheme> .

<https://signals.zndx.org/sdg#SDG_ICE_DIRECTIVE_SLAVIC_LINGUISTIC_ROOT> a skos:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "Slavic Linguistic Root" ;
    skos:notation "3.2.9" ;
    skos:altLabel "SLAVIC_LINGUISTIC_ROOT" ;
    skos:altLabel "Slavic linguistic root" ;
    skos:altLabel "Proto-Slavic root" ;
    skos:altLabel "Slavic etymological root" ;
    skos:altLabel "historical Slavic root" ;
    skos:altLabel "Slavic language root" ;
    skos:definition "A Slavic linguistic root represents the foundational linguistic element from which specific Slavic languages and dialects evolve, preserving the historical continuity of vocabulary and grammatical structures. Researchers utilize this term when tracing etymological lineages, reconstructing proto-forms, or analyzing the historical development of Slavic language families. The root serves as the primary unit of comparison in comparative linguistics, enabling scholars to map phonological shifts and semantic changes across time. A language is classified as a historical root for Slavic linguistic development. (Normative/Classificatory) A language operates as the historical root for Slavic linguistic development. (Procedural/Functional) Applied in historical linguistics and philology to identify the ancestral linguistic forms or roots that serve as the foundation for the development of Slavic languages and their dialects." ;
    skos:broader <https://signals.zndx.org/sdg#SDG_ICE_DIRECTIVE> ;
    skos:inScheme <https://signals.zndx.org/sdg/scheme> .

<https://signals.zndx.org/sdg#SDG_PROCESS_SOCIAL_HARMONY_RESTORATION> a skos:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "Social Harmony Restoration" ;
    skos:notation "1.108" ;
    skos:altLabel "SOCIAL_HARMONY_RESTORATION" ;
    skos:altLabel "Social harmony restoration" ;
    skos:altLabel "Social harmony act" ;
    skos:altLabel "Harmony restoration act" ;
    skos:altLabel "Social network restoration" ;
    skos:altLabel "Social harmony process" ;
    skos:definition "A social act that restores harmony within a social network. This act involves the deliberate actions taken to re-establish positive relationships and stability within the group. A social act that operates to restore harmony within a social network constitutes the defined phenomenon. The restoration of harmony within a social network is performed by a social act. Applies to a social act that restores harmony within a social network." ;
    skos:broader <https://signals.zndx.org/sdg#SDG_PROCESS> ;
    skos:inScheme <https://signals.zndx.org/sdg/scheme> .

<https://signals.zndx.org/sdg#SDG_PROCESS_SOCIAL_MEDIA_ACCOUNT_MANAGEMENT_PROCESS_DEFINITION> a skos:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "Social Media Account Management Process" ;
    skos:notation "1.109" ;
    skos:altLabel "SOCIAL_MEDIA_ACCOUNT_MANAGEMENT_PROCESS_DEFINITION" ;
    skos:altLabel "SocialMediaAccountManagementProcess" ;
    skos:definition "A process is defined as the component that manages account authorization records for social networking services. The management of account authorization records for social networking services is carried out by a process. Account authorization records for social networking services are managed by a process." ;
    skos:broader <https://signals.zndx.org/sdg#SDG_PROCESS> ;
    skos:inScheme <https://signals.zndx.org/sdg/scheme> .

<https://signals.zndx.org/sdg#SDG_GENERIC_SOCIAL_NETWORKING_SERVICE_TYPE> a skos:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "Social Networking Service Type" ;
    skos:notation "0.21" ;
    skos:altLabel "SOCIAL_NETWORKING_SERVICE_TYPE" ;
    skos:altLabel "SocialNetworkingServiceType" ;
    skos:definition "A service type functions as the category that encompasses social networking service usage. Social networking service usage falls within the scope of a service type. The designation of a service type applies to cases covering social networking service usage." ;
