    skos:definition "This term covers structured appraisal procedures used for standardized evaluation in professional or organizational contexts. Practitioners employ these methods to measure performance, verify compliance, or analyze outcomes using consistent criteria. The procedures rely on established protocols to ensure reliable and comparable results across different evaluation settings. An act of appraisal is defined as an activity utilized for standardized evaluation. To conduct an act of appraisal, one applies it for standardized evaluation. Applies to structured appraisal procedures used for standardized evaluation in professional or organizational contexts." ;
